Kitty i686 Operating system
*************************************************
Imagine someone so unemployeed he made an entire,
non Linux-based operating system for his cat
hehehhehe >:]
-----------------------------------------------
KittyOS needs an ix86 processor (compiled
with i686-elf-gcc). HOWEVER,
x86_64 (or amd64) is still supported via
instruction retrocompatibility!!
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
KittyOS needs to be compiled on arch-based
systems as Arch, CachyOS, Manjaro, etc.
It includes a nice installer called devmkiso.
ALWAYS use devmkiso to build instead of manual
compilation. You find the steps for the manual
compilation in the devmkiso script (as it is
a normal Bourne Again SHell script >:D)
devmkiso requires the following packages:
GRand Unified BootLoader (you don't need to
install GRUB as your bootloader,
you just need the package)
i686-elf-gcc located in ~/opt/cross/* (you
can either compile it yourself
our check out lordmiiko's repo
to grab a precompiled one)
A file editor specified in the EDITOR
enviroment variable
QEMU (to launch it on a VM,
completely optional)
